                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "5 months ago",
                        "rating":  2,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "We were planning to go to a restaurant on our shortlist for New Year\u0027s Eve with the kids, but by almost 8 pm, they\u0027d already been open for at least 2 or 3 hours! We wanted some soup, but it was all gone! No refills? The chicken leg wasn\u0027t very good, and my son didn\u0027t finish it! The sausages... we knew they\u0027d be made to order and take a while, but the wait was way too long...it didn\u0027t arrive until around 9 pm, and we even heard the kitchen asking the counter, \"Have the sausages arrived?\" Finally, my husband saw others participating in a raffle and said we could try our luck too! Turns out we were ignored! What?! ?! They\u0027re open on New Year\u0027s Eve?! And how can they treat customers who come in looking forward to a pleasant meal like this? Wouldn\u0027t it be better if they didn\u0027t want to open?!",
                                     "languageCode":  "en-US"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
                                             "text":  "想說跨年夜跟小孩來去口袋名單吃，結果7點快8點都開店至少2、3小時了吧？想喝湯發現到底了！沒補？雞腿味道不太好結果兒子沒吃完！香腸~知道現點現做要等，可也等太久....9點左右才上桌，中間還聽到廚房問櫃檯說：香腸去了嗎？最後先生看到別人抽獎就說我們也可以抽獎阿！原來我們被忽略了！甚麼？！？！跨年夜居然開店，開了怎麼是這樣對待懷著開心的心情進去想好好享受用餐時光的客人，有種既然不情願就不要開店不是更好嗎~的想法==",
                                             "languageCode":  "zh-Hant"
                                         },
